<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>EPC 153-22</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Schemes & Rules</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">EPC 153-22</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>EPC 153-22</strong> is the European Payments Council guidance document <em>"Provision of Addresses under the EPC Payment Schemes"</em>. Now at <strong>v2.1 (October 2025)</strong>, it defines when payer and payee addresses are required in SEPA payments, codifies the structured and hybrid formats, and records the cutover alignment to <strong>15 November 2026</strong>.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How EPC 153-22 works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>The document is guidance that operationalises the scheme rulebooks: it explains the non-EEA condition for payer addresses, states that only the structured Town and Country fields are needed for regulatory screening, and documents the amendment of the originally announced cutover date to the SR 2026 weekend (15 November 2026).</p></div> <p class="src">Source: EPC 153-22 v2.1 (October 2025); EPC 153-22 v2.1; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §10.6.1.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
